# verdict: satisfiable
# Source: ty mdtest call/function.md:184
#   Call expression / Generic overloaded callable constraints in constructors
# ty: `map(convert, ["a"])` should be map[Result[str]] (TODO, astral-sh/ty#2799).
# Today ty reveals map[Unknown]. The test prose says the cause: an overload
# that the constructor rejects leaves a mapping for its type variable, and that
# mapping then rejects the accepted overload.
#
#   T = TypeVar("T", str, bytes)
#   class Result(Generic[T])
#   convert: overload of [T](value: T) -> Result[T]
#                    and [T](value: Result[T]) -> Result[T]
#   map.__new__(cls, func: Callable[[_T1], _S], iterable: Iterable[_T1], /) -> map[_S]
#
# The `map` call gives _T1 and _S fresh metavariables. `convert` is an
# overloaded value checked against (?T1) -> ?S, so it is an `or` over its
# signatures. Each signature is generic with the constrained T, so each keeps
# its `forall` with the exact set {str, bytes}. The solver must pick a
# signature and a member of the exact set. The list gives ?T1 the lower bound
# str. The first signature with T = str fits. The second signature needs str
# to fit Result[T], which fails for both members. The intended reveal is an
# upper bound on the result, and map is invariant, so ?S must equal
# Result[str].
#
# Overload order: for an argument of type str, only the first signature fits.
# First match gives the same result as any match.
# Variance: map and Result use legacy type variables without a variance flag,
# so both are invariant.
# Approximations: Iterable is a nominal class. Only the one-iterable overload of
# `map.__new__` takes these arguments, so the other overloads and the `strict`
# keyword are dropped. The display ["a"] has its own type, list[str].
class str;
class bytes;
class Iterable[+T];
class list[T] extends Iterable[T];
class Result[T];
class map[S];
metavar ?T1;
metavar ?S;

assert map_func: (forall T in {str, bytes}. (T) -> Result[T] <: (?T1) -> ?S)
    or (forall T in {str, bytes}. (Result[T]) -> Result[T] <: (?T1) -> ?S);
assert map_iterable: list[str] <: Iterable[?T1];
assert map_result: map[?S] <: map[Result[str]];
